<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 345 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 345 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 345 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			     EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT  LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE     1.25 BLN   1.35 BLN   1.5 BLN   1.5 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY	700 MLN   1.05 BLN   1.45 BLN  1.795 BLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS	=	  350 MLN*   74 MLN     =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS     258 MLN*  =	    21 MLN     =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO FEB 17/18 442 MLN#  =	    =	    =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE				   345 MLN</p>
<p> * INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p> # INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
